1
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,490
But this...

2
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,950
Initiating docking procedures.

3
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:22,160
Roger.

4
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:36,170
Elevating from 6 to 9
on the Torino Scale!

5
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,390
CITY A – HERO ASSOCIATION HQ

6
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:46,390
The course suddenly shifted?

7
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:48,770
I see.

8
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:52,190
Then we will discuss how best
to deal with the situation.

9
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,150
Should I go now?

10
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:56,980
All right.

11
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:00,820
Master, for some reason
the Hero Association

12
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:02,080
wants me to come in.

13
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,370
I will be back later.

14
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,450
Okay. Maybe you're getting fired?

15
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:18,970
THE ULTIMATE DISCIPLE

16
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:32,060
One punch

17
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:37,520
Three, two, one, kill shot

18
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:41,280
sanjou, hisshou, shijou saikyou

19
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:41,280
He joins the fight, he wins, the strongest in history

20
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,280
nan datten da, frustration

21
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,280
Are you talking to him? Frustration

22
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,780
ore wa tomaranai

23
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,780
He's not going to stop

24
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:48,910
one punch, kanryou, rensenrenshou

25
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:48,910
One punch, that's it, one fight after another

26
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:52,540
ore wa katsu, tsune ni katsu, asshou

27
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:52,540
He wins, he always wins, overwhelmingly

28
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:56,370
power, get power

29
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:56,370
Power, get power

30
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:59,340
girigiri genkai made

31
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:59,340
On to the very edge

32
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:00,550
Hero

33
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:03,710
ore o tataeru koe ya

34
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:03,710
There are voices praising him

35
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,760
kassai nante hoshiku wa nai sa

36
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,760
but he's not doing this for acclaim

37
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,010
Hero

38
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:12,770
dakara hitoshirezu aku to tatakau

39
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:12,770
So he just fight evil without end

40
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:14,230
Nobody knows who he is

41
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:18,400
sora ooi oshiyoseru teki

42
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:18,400
Enemies to fight are numerous as the stars

43
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:18,440
{OP Sync Point - Smiley Star, First Frame}

44
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,480
ore wa se wo muke wa shinai

45
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,480
and he's not gonna turn his back on you

46
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,820
Hero

47
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:27,820
naraba yuruginaki kakugo shita tame

48
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:27,820
He's made up his mind and ain't gonna yield

49
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:35,040
tatakau hero

50
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:35,040
A fighting hero

51
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:41,590
kodoku na hero

52
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:41,590
A lone hero

53
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:37,880
I

54
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:38,540
I

55
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:39,170
I

56
00:02:39,170 --> 00:02:40,130
I

57
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:40,800
I

58
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,340
I

59
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:46,590
i wanna be a saikyou hero

60
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:46,590
I wanna be the strongest hero

61
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:51,520
CITY Z HERO ASSOCIATION BUILDING

62
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,060
Ah, you would be Genos?

63
00:02:57,830 --> 00:03:01,360
My name is Bang. Nice to meet you.

64
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:05,650
Bang, Class S rank 3,
a.k.a. "Silver Fang."

65
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:08,280
He possesses true skill.

66
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:10,950
The Association called me in.

67
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:15,040
Everyone's at Headquarters.

68
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:17,010
This little branch office
is empty just now.

69
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:19,920
Each of the Class S heroes
got the call to come here,

70
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:22,500
but we're the only ones
who showed up.

71
00:03:22,610 --> 00:03:23,800
Why is that?

72
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:28,180
Too far away, or perhaps they're busy.

73
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:32,100
Of course, some of the more
cold-blooded  ones simply don't bother.

74
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,180
After all, we're called up only

75
00:03:35,180 --> 00:03:38,440
when there's some impossible problem
they want us to take care of.

76
00:03:39,370 --> 00:03:41,650
Today's no exception.

77
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:46,400
The threat level is Dragon,
a worst-case scenario.

78
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:51,030
35 minutes from now,
a huge meteor will strike City Z.

79
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:55,580
They are asking if nearby Class S
heroes can do anything about it.

80
00:03:56,010 --> 00:03:57,160
A meteor?

81
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,000
Apparently, it suddenly changed paths.

82
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,920
That means the end for us.

83
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,590
The impact will wipe out City Z.

84
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,260
I'm afraid there's nothing
we can do this time.

85
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:13,100
You too should think about
evacuating with your loved ones.

86
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,060
Do the citizens know?

87
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:19,270
I was told they would estimate
the impact area

88
00:04:19,270 --> 00:04:22,020
and issue evacuation orders
30 minutes before it hits.

89
00:04:23,210 --> 00:04:27,740
Attention! This is an announcement
from the Hero Association.

90
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,830
People are sure to panic.

91
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,320
And you, old fellow?

92
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:34,030
"Old fellow", is it?

93
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:36,040
Call me Bang.

94
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,370
You are not evacuating?

95
00:04:37,890 --> 00:04:41,040
My dojo has been in my family
for generations.

96
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,460
I cannot abandon it.

97
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,670
"Fist of Flowing Water
Crushing Rock."

98
00:04:47,770 --> 00:04:48,880
Heard of it?

99
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,640
He left...

100
00:04:55,890 --> 00:04:57,930
Emergency evacuation warning.

101
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:00,020
The threat level is Dragon.

102
00:05:00,330 --> 00:05:02,810
Evacuate immediately.

103
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:07,190
21 more minutes
until meteor impact.

104
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,070
It's huge...

105
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:12,490
No way we can escape that.

106
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:20,960
So many people have
given up hope of survival.

107
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,080
It is not just City Z
that is in danger.

108
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,210
The neighboring cities will
also sustain damage.

109
00:05:25,850 --> 00:05:28,050
It is too late to evacuate.

110
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:32,390
I did not expect to be testing
this prototype so soon!

111
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,950
Let me see if an attack from
my incineration cannon at full power

112
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,910
will do the trick.

113
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,740
Master Saitama lives here too.

114
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,250
I cannot possibly
evacuate without him.

115
00:06:05,850 --> 00:06:07,000
Is that...?

116
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:20,600
You are Bofoi, correct?

117
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:24,400
And you are the new boy, Genos.

118
00:06:24,910 --> 00:06:26,980
Come to stop the meteor?

119
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:27,980
Yes.

120
00:06:28,670 --> 00:06:30,110
Class S rank 7.

121
00:06:30,170 --> 00:06:31,900
A hero who uses intense firepower

122
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:34,410
to obliterate his opponents along
with everything in their vicinity.

123
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,780
Does he also live in City Z?

124
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:39,450
Or did he rush here,
putting his life at risk?

125
00:06:39,970 --> 00:06:42,750
Bofoi. I need your help.

126
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:44,000
I refuse.

127
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Why?

128
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:49,210
I only came to field test
my new weapon.

129
00:06:49,270 --> 00:06:51,550
The meteor is a perfect target.

130
00:06:51,770 --> 00:06:52,970
A test?

131
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:55,220
If that meteor hits,
you too will die.

132
00:06:55,610 --> 00:06:57,760
– I will not.
– What?

133
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:03,020
What you are talking to right now
is a remotely-controlled drone.

134
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:06,650
Sorry to disappoint you,
but my life's not at stake here.

135
00:07:07,330 --> 00:07:11,020
Also, I am not Bofoi.
I am "Metal Knight."

136
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:14,400
Heroes call each other by
their hero names, not real names.

137
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,860
Everyone knows that.

138
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:21,160
Looks like it's time to
end our little chat.

139
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:27,460
All right!

140
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:30,540
Firing missiles!

141
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,010
Metal Knight?

142
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,470
I cannot fire with his missiles
in the way.

143
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:55,900
Amazing.

144
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,950
Such destructive power.

145
00:07:58,170 --> 00:07:59,490
This hero is dangerous.

146
00:07:59,550 --> 00:08:01,280
I must be wary.

147
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:14,420
Not quite potent enough, eh?

148
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:18,720
33 seconds left until impact.

149
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:21,220
To fire my incineration cannon
at full power,

150
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:23,260
I need five seconds to charge it
with my body's energy.

151
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:27,350
But the target is already close.

152
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:30,440
And if I do take it out, what then?

153
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:34,110
The meteor may break apart
and still cause a disaster.

154
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:35,110
But even before that,

155
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:37,070
will my weapons
be powerful enough to stop it?

156
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:40,360
Even Metal Knight's countless
missiles had no effect.

157
00:08:41,370 --> 00:08:43,120
First off, be calm.

158
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,540
I see you've lost composure.

159
00:08:45,970 --> 00:08:50,000
You are far too young
to be worried about failure.

160
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:54,000
When your back's up against
the wall, just muddle through.

161
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:56,000
The outcome won't change.

162
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,920
So that's what is best.

163
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:01,260
Muddling through is best...?

164
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:11,560
He is right.

165
00:09:12,450 --> 00:09:15,110
If the outcome will not change...

166
00:09:17,210 --> 00:09:21,160
then I how can I die
without giving it my all?

167
00:09:23,050 --> 00:09:24,620
Bang, get down!

168
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:26,410
Oh.

169
00:09:26,470 --> 00:09:29,040
I will no longer think about
failure or repercussions!

170
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:32,170
I will just pour everything I have...

171
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:34,000
...into one last shot!

172
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:48,100
Dammit, it is not working!

173
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:51,480
No! I think I see the meteor
being pushed back.

174
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,980
Really?

175
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,980
Oh, no. It was just my imagination.

176
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,070
You old fool!

177
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:02,030
So this...will be my grave.

178
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:14,540
Nine more seconds.

179
00:10:14,890 --> 00:10:17,130
Get out of here, Bang.

180
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,170
Old man, take care of Genos.

181
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:29,390
Who...who are you?

182
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,890
I'm a hero.

183
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,820
Master?!

184
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,830
You're not...

185
00:10:52,850 --> 00:10:54,080
gonna fall...

186
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:56,540
on my town!

187
00:11:08,070 --> 00:11:10,140
He shattered it!

188
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,720
Unbelievable!

189
00:11:11,990 --> 00:11:13,140
But...

190
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:24,570
It's collapsing...!

191
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:27,410
It's not just this building.

192
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:31,740
The destruction is spreading
through the whole city.

193
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:41,750
Guess that settles that.

194
00:11:54,310 --> 00:11:56,810
THREE DAYS LATER

195
00:11:55,980 --> 00:12:00,400
Although City Z was able to
avoid total destruction,

196
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,900
the city was still devastated,

197
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:07,200
with the effects of the meteor
fragments visible everywhere.

198
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:10,910
If only the Hero
Association had called...

199
00:12:10,910 --> 00:12:12,830
you to help instead of me, Master.

200
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:16,040
If you had worked
with Metal Knight,

201
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:18,580
the damage
could have been minimized.

202
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:21,210
But that Metal Knight guy...

203
00:12:21,210 --> 00:12:23,130
wasn't interested
in helping, right?

204
00:12:23,770 --> 00:12:25,050
So stop worrying about it.

205
00:12:25,770 --> 00:12:27,760
I think we kept the damage
to a minimum.

206
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:29,970
After all, no one died.

207
00:12:30,650 --> 00:12:31,800
He is right.

208
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:35,730
Master's punch killed
the meteor's momentum.

209
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:39,100
Theoretically, the shockwaves
from the meteor

210
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:41,230
would have annihilated everything.

211
00:12:41,330 --> 00:12:43,730
Stopping it was nothing
short of a miracle.

212
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,320
I would not be surprised

213
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:47,990
if people talk about Master
for years to come,

214
00:12:47,990 --> 00:12:49,990
praising him as a man of courage.

215
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,950
But Master has no idea.

216
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:56,910
Some of the public is even
making him out to be the bad guy

217
00:12:56,910 --> 00:13:00,040
for causing the partial
destruction of City Z.

218
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:03,960
No, I should not mention it.

219
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,050
By the way,

220
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:08,010
do you think we moved up in ranking?

221
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,130
Yes, we did.

222
00:13:10,570 --> 00:13:13,010
I went from Class S rank 17 to 16.

223
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,810
Metal Knight also moved up
from rank 7 to 6.

224
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:21,020
Master, you shot up from
Class C rank 342 to 5.

225
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:22,940
Number 5?!

226
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:25,070
From 342 to 5?

227
00:13:25,070 --> 00:13:27,990
What the hell?! That's crazy!

228
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,900
Not at all.

229
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,950
Your performance was worthy
of Class A or even Class S.

230
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:36,120
After all, it was threat level Dragon.

231
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:37,660
Yeah?

232
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,120
If there had been no damage,

233
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:41,540
I am sure you would be
at Class S rank 5.

234
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:47,340
Smashing the meteor alone
was worthy of Class A.

235
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,760
But I think the Hero Association
assumed that

236
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:55,100
Metal Knight and I played a big role.

237
00:13:55,450 --> 00:13:58,270
By the way,
they always report threat levels

238
00:13:58,270 --> 00:14:00,390
as "demon" or "tiger"
or whatever.

239
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,980
Does all that mean anything?

240
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,650
It does...

241
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:08,020
Tiger: A crisis threatening
massive loss of life.

242
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:11,240
Demon: A crisis threatening
to halt the functioning of an entire city,

243
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,110
or its destruction.

244
00:14:13,630 --> 00:14:16,660
Dragon: A crisis threatening
the destruction of multiple cities.

245
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,790
God: A crisis threatening
human extinction.

246
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:25,000
GUIDE TO THREAT LEVELS

247
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:22,910
Wow...I had no idea.

248
00:14:22,910 --> 00:14:26,210
I believe heroes often
consider threat levels

249
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:28,840
when deciding to respond or not.

250
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:31,880
But I guess
they do not matter to you.

251
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,890
Well, of course not.

252
00:14:34,530 --> 00:14:36,970
If the heroes run away,
who's left to help?

253
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,520
What are you doing?

254
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,690
I must record your words.

255
00:14:46,250 --> 00:14:49,980
Anyway, it wasn't all that much
for such a huge jump in rank...

256
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:51,740
All right.

257
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,030
I'll be out for a bit.

258
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:57,740
You are going out, Master?

259
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,700
I will come with you.

260
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:01,240
You stay here.

261
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:03,910
If something happens,
you'll get all the credit again.

262
00:15:11,900 --> 00:15:14,170
This place has been wrecked...

263
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:17,230
Oh.

264
00:15:17,230 --> 00:15:19,140
My favorite supermarket
got smashed.

265
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,930
And the crappy apartment building
I got kicked out of is...

266
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:24,770
Just fine...damn.

267
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:26,810
Hey.

268
00:15:28,330 --> 00:15:30,280
You cheating bastard.

269
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:33,110
Uh...who are you?

270
00:15:33,630 --> 00:15:36,150
You know damn well
I'm Tank-top Tiger!

271
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,870
Brother!

272
00:15:39,130 --> 00:15:40,700
It's that guy!

273
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:43,120
Seriously, who is this guy?

274
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:46,960
You called me, little bro?

275
00:15:47,770 --> 00:15:48,750
Brother!

276
00:15:48,890 --> 00:15:51,840
The hero Tank-top
Black Hole...

277
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:52,760
is here!

278
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:56,010
So you're the fraud who
takes credit for work done

279
00:15:56,010 --> 00:15:58,410
by Class S heroes in order
to jump the rankings?

280
00:15:58,410 --> 00:15:59,390
What the—?

281
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:02,640
No one could move up
to number five so quickly

282
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,730
without cheating.

283
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:07,230
What do you guys want?

284
00:16:07,230 --> 00:16:09,480
Huh? Isn't that obvious?

285
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,110
To beat you up so bad...

286
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:13,320
- you'll never be able to—
- Hang on, little bro.

287
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:18,150
Bastards like him don't learn
from that kind of lesson.

288
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,990
Let's make him really pay...

289
00:16:21,130 --> 00:16:24,040
with the most brutal method there is.

290
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:27,830
Are you the one?!

291
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:31,670
The jerk-off responsible
for destroying this city?!

292
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:34,800
I get it!

293
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:38,130
There are tons of people in this city
who are angry with him.

294
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,010
Unbelievable!

295
00:16:40,010 --> 00:16:41,890
How can you show your face?!

296
00:16:41,890 --> 00:16:43,390
I see what he's doing.

297
00:16:43,390 --> 00:16:45,600
He's going to use their anger...

298
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:49,350
Do you feel nothing at
the sight of this devastation?

299
00:16:50,830 --> 00:16:53,020
...to break his spirit!

300
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,280
You're gloating,

301
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:57,990
thinking you've actually
saved these people!

302
00:16:57,990 --> 00:17:01,780
Why else would you be walking around
so shamelessly?

303
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:03,780
Thanks to your screw up,

304
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:07,210
these citizens have nowhere to go!

305
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,080
If you were gonna fail this hard,
why'd you butt in?!

306
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:14,170
The other heroes would
have done a way better job!

307
00:17:14,170 --> 00:17:16,050
And yet you still wanna play hero,

308
00:17:16,050 --> 00:17:18,220
even after causing such
a huge disaster?

309
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:19,970
Look at this place!

310
00:17:19,970 --> 00:17:22,800
All this destruction is your doing!

311
00:17:25,070 --> 00:17:25,970
That's right.

312
00:17:26,910 --> 00:17:28,520
I-It's your fault!

313
00:17:29,910 --> 00:17:31,390
They took the bait.

314
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:33,450
You hear that?

315
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:36,270
The heart-wrenching cry
of someone who lost his home!

316
00:17:36,370 --> 00:17:42,030
Look at them all, victims of
your thoughtless actions!

317
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:43,410
That's right!

318
00:17:43,410 --> 00:17:44,950
Yeah, you tell him!

319
00:17:44,950 --> 00:17:47,620
Haven't you even thought
to take responsibility?

320
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,700
Yeah!

321
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:50,080
You're inhuman!

322
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:53,080
Give up being a hero!

323
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:56,040
Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!

324
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,340
Give it up!

325
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:59,630
- Give it up!
- Give it up!

326
00:17:59,630 --> 00:18:00,630
Give it up!

327
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:01,630
Give it up!

328
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:03,720
- Give it up!
- Go on, get outta here!

329
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,760
- Give it up!
- Get lost!

330
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:05,930
- Give it up!
- Beat it!

331
00:18:05,930 --> 00:18:06,970
- Give it up!
- Scram!

332
00:18:06,970 --> 00:18:08,890
- Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up!

333
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:12,060
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!

334
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:15,270
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!

335
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:18,530
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!

336
00:18:18,530 --> 00:18:21,690
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up! Give it up!

337
00:18:21,690 --> 00:18:23,820
- Give it up! Give it up!
- Give it up! Give it up!

338
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:24,950
We got him.

339
00:18:24,950 --> 00:18:27,920
His pride should be
shattered by now.

340
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,830
That's what he gets for cheating...

341
00:18:29,930 --> 00:18:30,910
That idiot!

342
